by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-15T12:28:38Z

Answering the question that sat with me since May, sorry for the wait: no, not worth it, let's keep the `@method` annotations on the existing interfaces.

You are right on the conceptual point, and it is the criterion that matters. Interface segregation earns its keep when the capability is orthogonal to the base contract, `ResetInterface` being the house example. Steps are not orthogonal to a form flow, they are its essence: every implementer of `FormFlowBuilderInterface` deals with steps or has no reason to implement it. Three parallel interfaces would also force `instanceof` branching at every call site of the new methods, and after 9.0 merges the methods in, the extra interfaces would remain as permanent vestiges. The `@method` plus upgrade-note path is the established one for exactly this case.

